#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:1
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:3
msgid "`nix-env --query` - display information about packages"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:5
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-env` {`--query` | `-q`} _names…_ \\[`--installed` | `--available` | `-"
"a`\\] \\[{`--status` | `-s`}\\] \\[{`--attr-path` | `-P`}\\] \\[`--no-"
"name`\\] \\[{`--compare-versions` | `-c`}\\] \\[`--system`\\] \\[`--drv-"
"path`\\] \\[`--out-path`\\] \\[`--description`\\] \\[`--meta`\\] \\[`--"
"xml`\\] \\[`--json`\\] \\[{`--prebuilt-only` | `-b`}\\] \\[{`--attr` | `-A`} "
"_attribute-path_\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:23
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:25
msgid ""
"The query operation displays information about either the store paths that "
"are installed in the current generation of the active profile (`--"
"installed`), or the derivations that are available for installation in the "
"active Nix expression (`--available`). It only prints information about "
"derivations whose symbolic name matches one of _names_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:31
msgid "The derivations are sorted by their `name` attributes."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:33
msgid "Source selection"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:35
msgid ""
"The following flags specify the set of things on which the query operates."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:38
msgid "`--installed`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:40
msgid ""
"The query operates on the store paths that are installed in the current "
"generation of the active profile. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:43
msgid "`--available` / `-a`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:45
msgid ""
"The query operates on the derivations that are available in the active Nix "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:48
msgid "Queries"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:50
msgid ""
"The following flags specify what information to display about the selected "
"derivations. Multiple flags may be specified, in which case the information "
"is shown in the order given here. Note that the name of the derivation is "
"shown unless `--no-name` is specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:55
msgid "`--xml`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:57
msgid ""
"Print the result in an XML representation suitable for automatic processing "
"by other tools. The root element is called `items`, which contains a `item` "
"element for each available or installed derivation. The fields discussed "
"below are all stored in attributes of the `item` elements."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:63
msgid "`--json`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:65
msgid ""
"Print the result in a JSON representation suitable for automatic processing "
"by other tools."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:68
msgid "`--prebuilt-only` / `-b`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:70
msgid ""
"Show only derivations for which a substitute is registered, i.e., there is a "
"pre-built binary available that can be downloaded in lieu of building the "
"derivation. Thus, this shows all packages that probably can be installed "
"quickly."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:75
msgid "`--status` / `-s`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:77
msgid ""
"Print the _status_ of the derivation. The status consists of three "
"characters. The first is `I` or `-`, indicating whether the derivation is "
"currently installed in the current generation of the active profile. This is "
"by definition the case for `--installed`, but not for `--available`. The "
"second is `P` or `-`, indicating whether the derivation is present on the "
"system. This indicates whether installation of an available derivation will "
"require the derivation to be built. The third is `S` or `-`, indicating "
"whether a substitute is available for the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:87
msgid "`--attr-path` / `-P`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:89
msgid ""
"Print the _attribute path_ of the derivation, which can be used to "
"unambiguously select it using the `--attr` option available in commands that "
"install derivations like `nix-env --install`. This option only works "
"together with `--available`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:94
msgid "`--no-name`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:96
msgid "Suppress printing of the `name` attribute of each derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:98
msgid "`--compare-versions` / `-c`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:100
msgid ""
"Compare installed versions to available versions, or vice versa (if `--"
"available` is given). This is useful for quickly seeing whether upgrades for "
"installed packages are available in a Nix expression. A column is added with "
"the following meaning:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:105
msgid "`<` _version_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:107
msgid "A newer version of the package is available or installed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:109
msgid "`=` _version_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:111
msgid "At most the same version of the package is available or installed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:114
msgid "`>` _version_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:116
msgid "Only older versions of the package are available or installed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:118
msgid "`- ?`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:120
msgid "No version of the package is available or installed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:122
msgid "`--system`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:124
msgid "Print the `system` attribute of the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:126
msgid "`--drv-path`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:128
msgid ""
"Print the [store path](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-path) to the [store "
"derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-derivation)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:133
msgid "`--out-path`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:135
msgid "Print the output path of the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:137
msgid "`--description`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:139
msgid ""
"Print a short (one-line) description of the derivation, if available. The "
"description is taken from the `meta.description` attribute of the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:143
msgid "`--meta`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:145
msgid ""
"Print all of the meta-attributes of the derivation. This option is only "
"available with `--xml` or `--json`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:148
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:150
msgid ""
"The following options are allowed for all `nix-env` operations, but may not "
"always have an effect."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:152
msgid "`--file` / `-f` _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:154
msgid ""
"Specifies the Nix expression (designated below as the _active Nix "
"expression_) used by the `--install`, `--upgrade`, and `--query --available` "
"operations to obtain derivations. The default is `~/.nix-defexpr`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:159
msgid ""
"If the argument starts with `http://` or `https://`, it is interpreted as "
"the URL of a tarball that will be downloaded and unpacked to a temporary "
"location. The tarball must include a single top-level directory containing "
"at least a file named `default.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:164
msgid "`--profile` / `-p` _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:166
msgid ""
"Specifies the profile to be used by those operations that operate on a "
"profile (designated below as the _active profile_). A profile is a sequence "
"of user environments called _generations_, one of which is the _current "
"generation_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:171
msgid "`--dry-run`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:173
msgid ""
"For the `--install`, `--upgrade`, `--uninstall`, `--switch-generation`, `--"
"delete-generations` and `--rollback` operations, this flag will cause `nix-"
"env` to print what _would_ be done if this flag had not been specified, "
"without actually doing it."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:178
msgid ""
"`--dry-run` also prints out which paths will be [substituted](../../glossary."
"md) (i.e., downloaded) and which paths will be built from source (because no "
"substitute is available)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:182
msgid "`--system-filter` _system_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:184
msgid ""
"By default, operations such as `--query --available` show derivations "
"matching any platform. This option allows you to use derivations for the "
"specified platform _system_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:192
msgid "Common Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:194
msgid "Most Nix commands accept the following command-line options:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:196
msgid "<span id=\"opt-help\">[`--help`](#opt-help)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:198
msgid "Prints out a summary of the command syntax and exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:200
msgid "<span id=\"opt-version\">[`--version`](#opt-version)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:202
msgid "Prints out the Nix version number on standard output and exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:204
msgid ""
"For machine-readable output, including versions of the libraries Nix links "
"against, see the [`nix version`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md) "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:207
msgid "<span id=\"opt-verbose\">[`--verbose`](#opt-verbose)</span> / `-v`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:209
msgid ""
"Increases the level of verbosity of diagnostic messages printed on standard "
"error. For each Nix operation, the information printed on standard output is "
"well-defined; any diagnostic information is printed on standard error, never "
"on standard output."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:213
msgid ""
"This option may be specified repeatedly. Currently, the following verbosity "
"levels exist:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:216
msgid "`0` “Errors only”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:218
msgid "Only print messages explaining why the Nix invocation failed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:220
msgid "`1` “Informational”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:222
msgid "Print _useful_ messages about what Nix is doing. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:225
msgid "`2` “Talkative”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:227
msgid "Print more informational messages."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:229
msgid "`3` “Chatty”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:231
msgid "Print even more informational messages."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:233
msgid "`4` “Debug”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:235
msgid "Print debug information."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:237
msgid "`5` “Vomit”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:239
msgid "Print vast amounts of debug information."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:241
msgid "<span id=\"opt-quiet\">[`--quiet`](#opt-quiet)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:243
msgid ""
"Decreases the level of verbosity of diagnostic messages printed on standard "
"error. This is the inverse option to `-v` / `--verbose`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:246
msgid ""
"This option may be specified repeatedly. See the previous verbosity levels "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:249
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-log-format\">[`--log-format`](#opt-log-format)</span> _format_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:251
msgid ""
"This option can be used to change the output of the log format, with "
"_format_ being one of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:253
msgid "`raw`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:255
msgid "This is the raw format, as outputted by nix-build."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:257
msgid "`internal-json`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:259
msgid "Outputs the logs in a structured manner."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:261
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:263
msgid ""
"While the schema itself is relatively stable, the format of the error-"
"messages (namely of the `msg`\\-field) can change between releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:267
msgid "`bar`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:269
msgid "Only display a progress bar during the builds."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:271
msgid "`bar-with-logs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:273
msgid "Display the raw logs, with the progress bar at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:275
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-no-build-output\">[`--no-build-output`](#opt-no-build-"
"output)</span> / `-Q`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:277
msgid ""
"By default, output written by builders to standard output and standard error "
"is echoed to the Nix command's standard error. This option suppresses this "
"behaviour. Note that the builder's standard output and error are always "
"written to a log file in `prefix/nix/var/log/nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:281
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-jobs\">[`--max-jobs`](#opt-max-jobs)</span> / `-j` "
"_number_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:283
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of build jobs that Nix will perform in parallel to "
"the specified number. Specify `auto` to use the number of CPUs in the "
"system. The default is specified by the `max-jobs` configuration setting, "
"which itself defaults to `1`. A higher value is useful on SMP systems or to "
"exploit I/O latency."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:288
msgid ""
"Setting it to `0` disallows building on the local machine, which is useful "
"when you want builds to happen only on remote builders."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:290
msgid "<span id=\"opt-cores\">[`--cores`](#opt-cores)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:292
msgid ""
"Sets the value of the `NIX_BUILD_CORES` environment variable in the "
"invocation of builders. Builders can use this variable at their discretion "
"to control the maximum amount of parallelism. For instance, in Nixpkgs, if "
"the derivation attribute `enableParallelBuilding` is set to `true`, the "
"builder passes the `-jN` flag to GNU Make. It defaults to the value of the "
"`cores` configuration setting, if set, or `1` otherwise. The value `0` means "
"that the builder should use all available CPU cores in the system."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:298
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-silent-time\">[`--max-silent-time`](#opt-max-silent-"
"time)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:300
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of seconds that a builder can go without producing "
"any data on standard output or standard error. The default is specified by "
"the `max-silent-time` configuration setting. `0` means no time-out."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:304
msgid "<span id=\"opt-timeout\">[`--timeout`](#opt-timeout)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:306
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of seconds that a builder can run. The default is "
"specified by the `timeout` configuration setting. `0` means no timeout."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:310
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-keep-going\">[`--keep-going`](#opt-keep-going)</span> / `-k`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:312
msgid ""
"Keep going in case of failed builds, to the greatest extent possible. That "
"is, if building an input of some derivation fails, Nix will still build the "
"other inputs, but not the derivation itself. Without this option, Nix stops "
"if any build fails (except for builds of substitutes), possibly killing "
"builds in progress (in case of parallel or distributed builds)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:316
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-keep-failed\">[`--keep-failed`](#opt-keep-failed)</span> / `-"
"K`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:318
msgid ""
"Specifies that in case of a build failure, the temporary directory (usually "
"in `/tmp`) in which the build takes place should not be deleted. The path of "
"the build directory is printed as an informational message."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:321
msgid "<span id=\"opt-fallback\">[`--fallback`](#opt-fallback)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:323
msgid ""
"Whenever Nix attempts to build a derivation for which substitutes are known "
"for each output path, but realising the output paths through the substitutes "
"fails, fall back on building the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:325
msgid ""
"The most common scenario in which this is useful is when we have registered "
"substitutes in order to perform binary distribution from, say, a network "
"repository. If the repository is down, the realisation of the derivation "
"will fail. When this option is specified, Nix will build the derivation "
"instead. Thus, installation from binaries falls back on installation from "
"source. This option is not the default since it is generally not desirable "
"for a transient failure in obtaining the substitutes to lead to a full build "
"from source (with the related consumption of resources)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:331
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-readonly-mode\">[`--readonly-mode`](#opt-readonly-mode)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:333
msgid ""
"When this option is used, no attempt is made to open the Nix database. Most "
"Nix operations do need database access, so those operations will fail."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:336
msgid "<span id=\"opt-arg\">[`--arg`](#opt-arg)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:338
msgid ""
"This option is accepted by `nix-env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-shell` and "
"`nix-build`. When evaluating Nix expressions, the expression evaluator will "
"automatically try to call functions that it encounters. It can automatically "
"call functions for which every argument has a [default value](../../language/"
"syntax.md#functions) (e.g., `{ argName ?  defaultValue }: ...`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:342
msgid ""
"With `--arg`, you can also call functions that have arguments without a "
"default value (or override a default value). That is, if the evaluator "
"encounters a function with an argument named _name_, it will call it with "
"value _value_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:345
msgid ""
"For instance, the top-level `default.nix` in Nixpkgs is actually a function:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:354
msgid ""
"So if you call this Nix expression (e.g., when you do `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname`), the function will be called automatically using the value "
"[`builtins.currentSystem`](../../language/builtins.md) for the `system` "
"argument. You can override this using `--arg`, e.g., `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname --arg system \\\"i686-freebsd\\\"`. (Note that since the "
"argument is a Nix string literal, you have to escape the quotes.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:358
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-arg-from-file\">[`--arg-from-file`](#opt-arg-from-file)</"
"span> _name_ _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:360
msgid ""
"Pass the contents of file _path_ as the argument _name_ to Nix functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:362
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-arg-from-stdin\">[`--arg-from-stdin`](#opt-arg-from-stdin)</"
"span> _name_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:364
msgid "Pass the contents of stdin as the argument _name_ to Nix functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:366
msgid "<span id=\"opt-argstr\">[`--argstr`](#opt-argstr)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:368
msgid ""
"This option is like `--arg`, only the value is not a Nix expression but a "
"string. So instead of `--arg system \\\"i686-linux\\\"` (the outer quotes "
"are to keep the shell happy) you can say `--argstr system i686-linux`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:371
msgid "<span id=\"opt-attr\">[`--attr`](#opt-attr)</span> / `-A` _attrPath_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:373
msgid ""
"Select an attribute from the top-level Nix expression being evaluated. (`nix-"
"env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` only.) The _attribute "
"path_ _attrPath_ is a sequence of attribute names separated by dots. For "
"instance, given a top-level Nix expression _e_, the attribute path `xorg."
"xorgserver` would cause the expression `e.xorg.xorgserver` to be used. See "
"[`nix-env --install`](../../command-ref/nix-env/install.md) for some "
"concrete examples."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:379
msgid ""
"In addition to attribute names, you can also specify array indices. For "
"instance, the attribute path `foo.3.bar` selects the `bar` attribute of the "
"fourth element of the array in the `foo` attribute of the top-level "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:384
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-eval-store\">[`--eval-store`](#opt-eval-store)</span> _store-"
"url_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:386
msgid ""
"The [URL to the Nix store](../../store/types/index.md#store-url-format) to "
"use for evaluation, i.e. where to store derivations (`.drv` files) and "
"inputs referenced by them."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:388
msgid "<span id=\"opt-expr\">[`--expr`](#opt-expr)</span> / `-E`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:390
msgid ""
"Interpret the command line arguments as a list of Nix expressions to be "
"parsed and evaluated, rather than as a list of file names of Nix "
"expressions. (`nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` only.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:393
msgid ""
"For `nix-shell`, this option is commonly used to give you a shell in which "
"you can build the packages returned by the expression. If you want to get a "
"shell which contain the _built_ packages ready for use, give your expression "
"to the `nix-shell --packages ` convenience flag instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/query.md:396
msgid "<span id=\"opt-I\">[`-I` / `--include`](#opt-I)</span> _path_"
msgstr ""

